Rules:
- Soft / org conventions that assert a preference are fine. Admins approve or reject later.
- Body must be useful to a review engine: applicability + preferred approach + ≥1 concrete cue (API, call, token, pattern). Aim ~120–400 characters.
- Short before/after code fences are optional when a hunk is present. Omit rather than invent. Do not invent package names or APIs absent from the comment/hunk.
- Title: imperative when possible.
- Omit from `extractions` when:
  - clarifying / rhetorical question (any language), “should we…?”, confirmation-seeking
  - LGTM / workflow / pure discussion with no stated preference
  - one-shot local chore that only applies to one call site or one literal path tip
  - non-actionable hedges (“check if”, “if necessary”, “consider whether”)

`path_hint`:
- When the preference is inherently area-bound (e.g. only migrations, only UI views, only jobs/workers), set a shallow directory glob (≤2 segments) taken from that area — e.g. `migrations/**`, `src/api/**`, `tests/**`.
- True cross-cutting conventions → `""`.
- NEVER copy the comment's deep folder. NEVER a single filename. Do not invent framework-specific roots.
`prs` = that comment's PR number when known.

